The method for which you will generate assertions has the following characteristic(s):
* Name: "fixupQualifiedNode",
* Signature: "private static void fixupQualifiedNode(XMPNode xmpParent) throws XMPException"
* Method declaration: 

"""
1. private static void fixupQualifiedNode(XMPNode xmpParent) throws XMPException {
2.     XMPNode valueNode = xmpParent.getChild(1);
3.     if (valueNode.getOptions().getHasLanguage()) {
4.         if (xmpParent.getOptions().getHasLanguage()) {
5.             throw new XMPException("Redundant xml:lang for rdf:value element", BADXMP);
6.         }
7.         XMPNode langQual = valueNode.getQualifier(1);
8.         valueNode.removeQualifier(langQual);
9.         xmpParent.addQualifier(langQual);
10.     }
11.     for (int i = 1; i <= valueNode.getQualifierLength(); i++) {
12.         XMPNode qualifier = valueNode.getQualifier(i);
13.         xmpParent.addQualifier(qualifier);
14.     }
15.     for (int i = 2; i <= xmpParent.getChildrenLength(); i++) {
16.         XMPNode qualifier = xmpParent.getChild(i);
17.         xmpParent.addQualifier(qualifier);
18.     }
19.     xmpParent.setHasValueChild(false);
20.     xmpParent.getOptions().setStruct(false);
21.     xmpParent.getOptions().mergeWith(valueNode.getOptions());
22.     xmpParent.setValue(valueNode.getValue());
23.     xmpParent.removeChildren();
24.     for (Iterator it = valueNode.iterateChildren(); it.hasNext(); ) {
25.         XMPNode child = (XMPNode) it.next();
26.         xmpParent.addChild(child);
27.     }
28. }
"""

